WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.570
-This is the first time
I´ve seen you since the Oscars.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations.
You have an Oscar.

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you. Thanks.
-That´s so great.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.941 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
It´s so well-deserved.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:09.175 size:84% position:42%
Where -- Do you mind --

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m assuming
you get asked this a lot.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:11.878
But where do you keep it?

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:13.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My mom has it.

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s very sweet.
-Yes.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:17.050
-Did she ask before she took it?
-No.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
-No, she did.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, nice.
So, do you have any --

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you didn´t want it
in your own home?

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:26.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
It felt a little strange.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:29.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I have two things
in my apartment

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are related
to that kind of idea,

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:34.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a Nickelodeon
Kids´ Choice Award,

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is an orange blimp
that is also a kaleidoscope.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s fantastic.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And my spelling-bee trophy
from the fourth grade.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got first place
in the spelling bee.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow! That´s really great.
-Yeah.

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:48.448 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:51.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you remember
your winning word?

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:54.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was trying to think
about this for a little while.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:57.657
And what I remember it to be --
I could be incorrect --

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
was a compound word,
which is "microfinance."

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Microfinance.
-Go ahead.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:09.002
-M-I-C-R-O-F-I-N-A-N-C-E.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now I have to
give you my trophy.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.441
The way --
When you asked me to spell it --

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don´t want
to sound like a jerk,

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that seems like
a super-easy word.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:18.878 size:88% position:44%
-It´s a super-easy word.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think I was also
like 10 years old.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:22.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, it was pretty easy.
It was a pretty easy word.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:24.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, what were people
going out on?

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like "mittens"?

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.956 size:78% position:39%
"Mittens" was before.
The guy who blew it.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That Josh.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
And "mittens."
He couldn´t handle it.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Still can´t wear mittens.
He´s so upset.

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:36.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know Josh.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:38.531 size:81% position:41%
-This is very exciting
that you got to work

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.266
with Billie Jean King because --

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:42.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
You actually
spent time with her.

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:43.970
And she was here last night,

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you guys went
to the U.S. Open together.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We did.
-And here is a photo

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:50.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
of you guys
enjoying each other´s company,

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.311
it seems like, right here.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really enjoying
each other´s company.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.147
-You seem very happy right here.

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.249
You´re enjoying her so much,
you want to obviously save it,

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:59.686
so you can enjoy her on the road
when she´s not with you.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:02.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
But she said she´s a very hard
person to watch tennis with

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:03.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
because she can´t stop talking
about what she´s seeing.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.725 size:84% position:42%
-But I think that´s why
she´s a great person

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
to watch tennis with.
-I would think the same.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:09.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I think
I´ve mentioned this before,

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:11.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there is no one
on Billie Jean´s other side,

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:15.135
so it´s just me, and she does
live commentary the entire time.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-Right in your ear.

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
And you did not mind?

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did not mind.
I was learning so much.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.708 size:75% position:38%
-Is she mostly happy

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.243 size:81% position:41%
with what she´s seeing
or mostly not happy?

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:25.879
-It depends. She just --
Every emotion she´s having

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.647 size:78% position:39%
goes in a live stream

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a bunch of facts
interspersed

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.383
of what´s actually happening.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:32.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Does it ever go outside
of tennis, like, "I´m hungry"?

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.654 size:81% position:41%
Does that ever happen?

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think -- Yeah,
I mean, she´s enthusiastic.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.158
-She´s just running everything.
-Yeah. It´s all coming through.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.593
-And she´s very enthusiastic.
I found her very inspiring.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:41.961
We were talking backstage.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:44.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
In our green room,
Billie Jean King was just --

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.799
Anybody who walked by her,
she would just grab and inspire.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:49.102
Like, she would walk by --
-He told me this backstage.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:50.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The person who was
putting her mic on.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was like, "Do you like
putting mics on?"

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.874
And she was like, "I do." And
she´s like, "Follow your dreams!

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
But if you ever
stop liking it --

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.244
If you ever stop liking it,
you go do something else!"

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.446
And I was like, "Wow.
She just really wants to get..."

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s her in a nutshell.
-Yeah.

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She inspires
everyone she meets.

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.451 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, she´s wonderful.
-She´s something else.

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.187 size:81% position:41%
-And you have never --
This is the first time

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:09.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you have played
a real person.

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. Correct.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.959
-So "La La Land," that means,
was not based on a true story.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.861
-It´s not based on a true story.
-None of that happened?

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It didn´t happen.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:17.864
-I have driven a Prius before.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:19.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s close enough for me.
-You know?

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.401
-So it´s based on a true story?

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:24.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It´s based -- It´s loosely
based on a true story.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What was it --
Did you find it --

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it extra burdensome
to play somebody who is real?

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.743
-I mean, yes, definitely.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:34.113
It was -- There is a fear factor
that goes into that.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:36.115
Because she´s going to sit down
and see it at the end.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:39.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, knowing that
is pretty daunting.

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also the fact
that I didn´t play tennis

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.922
before playing Billie Jean.

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then when
I went to meet her,

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:45.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
there was that precedent,

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
the, like, "Hi, I´m an actress
that´s playing you

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
that doesn´t play tennis
and I´m super shy."

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was like, "I´m super
shy. You´re playing me.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don´t play tennis.
What´s going on?"

00:03:51.965 --> 00:03:54.133
-What was the scene when you
first met Billie Jean King?

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I met her at her apartment.
She lives in New York.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:04:00.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was so sweet and warm
and inspiring instantly.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:03.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, she really keys in
on how to inspire you.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:05.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
So she brought me
up to her apartment,

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
and her partner, Ilana,
was there

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:09.215
drinking out of a mug that said
"It´s Good To Be King."

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:10.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fantastic.

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I was like, "It does seem
pretty good to be King."

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.

